# patch: 006-account-banner-chunked
# format: CHUNKED ONLY (2.1.242+). Monolithic trees keep using
#         006-account-banner.patch, which is unchanged.
# version: VERSION-INDEPENDENT. Verified apply-clean against the emitted-file
#          content of BOTH 2.1.263 and 2.1.260.
# depends: the PIN rule for utils/versionSuffix.ts (delivered as
#          /tmp/anchors-263/006-pin.json, to be merged into
#          tools-ts/anchor-rules.json). THIS PATCH DOES NOT APPLY WITHOUT IT --
#          without the pin there is no utils/versionSuffix.js in the tree.
# description: getVersionSuffix() returns ' [claudiverse]' so every version
#              readout is identifiably patched. This is the build's canary.
#
# ============================================================================
# RE-AUTHORED 2026-09-07 -- VERSION-LOCK RESOLVED BY A PIN, NOT BY A REWRITE
# ============================================================================
#
# WHAT WAS BROKEN, AND WHY NO HUNK COULD FIX IT:
#   The target is a standalone chunk that the emitter named by its MINIFIED
#   export, so the FILENAME ITSELF drifted every release:
#       2.1.260:  _unmatched/0003_Px.js
#       2.1.263:  _unmatched/0003_$x.js
#   `git apply` matches paths LITERALLY -- no glob, no fuzz, no rename
#   detection. The failure therefore happened in the `--- / +++` header BEFORE
#   a single context line was consulted. Anchoring inside the hunk, which is
#   what unblocked every other patch in this set, is inert against a path
#   mismatch. The FILE had to acquire a stable name.
#
# HOW IT IS FIXED:
#   A `type: "pin"` rule keyed on BUILD_REF_NAME gives that module the stable
#   path utils/versionSuffix.js at build step 2 (emitter.ts:48 calls
#   resolvePinRules), which is BEFORE patches are applied at step 3. This patch
#   targets the pinned path, so the minified name never appears in a path.
#   The pin key is a build-CONSTANT property KEY, not a build-varying value:
#   VERSION / BUILD_TIME / GIT_SHA sit in the very same object literal and
#   change every release, but BUILD_REF_NAME is an upstream source identifier
#   preserved by minification. MEASURED tree-unique -- exactly 1 manifest
#   section of 1650 on 2.1.263 and 1 of 1643 on 2.1.260.
#
# THE HUNK BODY IS VERSION-INDEPENDENT BY CONSTRUCTION:
#   Context is trimmed to `) {` and `}` and the changed line is `return '';`.
#   All three are BYTE-IDENTICAL on 2.1.263 and 2.1.260 (verified). Every
#   version-varying token in this file -- the minified name `$x`/`Px`, VERSION,
#   BUILD_TIME, GIT_SHA -- lives in the parameter object ABOVE the context
#   window and is never matched. The added line introduces no identifier at
#   all, only a string literal.
#
#   NOTE the `function $x(` text after the `@@` marker: that is git's function
#   -context hint, which `git apply` does NOT match against. VERIFIED by
#   positive control -- the patch applies cleanly to the 2.1.260 file, where
#   that function is named `Px`.
#
# 🔴 THE PIN CHANGES THIS FILE'S HEADER, so the patch is authored against the
#   PINNED emit, not against today's _unmatched/ file. A pinned module is
#   emitted with confidence "high", which routes it through beautify()
#   (emitter.ts) -- and beautify COLLAPSES the two blank lines in the Anthropic
#   banner that the unmatched file still carries. Measured: exactly 2 blank
#   lines removed, which shifts the hunk's start line from 22 to 20. Authoring
#   this against the current _unmatched/ file would have produced an off-by-two
#   that only surfaced after the pin landed.
#
# HOW THE EXPECTED FILE WAS DERIVED (reproducible):
#   The 2.1.263 and 2.1.260 module trees were regenerated from
#   versionref/2.1.263-bin and versionref/2.1.260-bin with
#   `tools/extract_chunks.py --splitter-compat` into a private scratch dir (the
#   shared .deob_cache was NOT touched -- it holds 2.1.238), then the emitted
#   content was reproduced by calling the pipeline's own beautify() followed by
#   prettifyCode() from tools-ts/src. That is the exact transform chain a real
#   build applies to a pinned module before step 3.
#
# ⚠️ WHAT IS NOT YET VERIFIED: no build has been run with the pin merged, so
#   utils/versionSuffix.js does not exist in any on-disk tree yet. The apply
#   check above is against the RECONSTRUCTED emit, not against build output.
#   The residual risk is that the real pipeline's step 2.6 renamer alters this
#   file (it would rename `$x`/`Px` if an anchor rule named it) -- the pin
#   itself emits no rename, and the shipped getVersionSuffix_* rules cannot
#   fire here (both declare hardcoded version-specific files with
#   no_tree_scan:true), so the expectation is no change to the context window.
#   Confirm on the first build after the pin merges.
#
diff --git a/utils/versionSuffix.js b/utils/versionSuffix.js
index 7db8d43..50b6857 100644
--- a/utils/versionSuffix.js
+++ b/utils/versionSuffix.js
@@ -20,3 +20,3 @@ function $x(
 ) {
-    return '';
+    return ' [claudiverse]';
 }
